\taxon{Remark}
\title{How we formulate an executable model artifact}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{pretraining}

\p{Section 6 of \citek{phuong2022formal} describes decoder architecture.
Sections 3.1 and 3.5 of \citek{kudo2018sentencepiece} treat the tokenizer as a
separate model. Public model releases additionally distribute weights,
configuration, and numerical conventions. We collect these runtime
ingredients in \ref{ftip-001K} because none alone determines an executable
next-token law.}

\p{Training provenance accompanies the artifact but is not itself a runtime
argument. Later causal claims must distinguish the executable endpoint from
the process that produced it.}
